# CLI↔MCP parity for every IDE

> **ABSOLUTE**: Skills and IDE bootstrap rules must work for **all** ax IDE targets whether MCP is connected or the project is CLI-only.

## Required

1. Prefer MCP tools when the ax MCP server is connected.
2. When MCP is unavailable or the project is CLI-only, use the matching CLI commands (`ax preflight`, `ax explore`, `ax session` / `ax turn`, `ax sync`, …) — do not skip graph/policy workflow.
3. `ax install --mode cli-only` must seed instruction surfaces for every supported IDE without writing MCP server configs.
4. Before claiming CLI-only/IDE parity is done, verify each IDE target gets the expected files and that MCP configs are absent.